Excavation: let Field/gathering gear reduce pickaxe break chance.

Retargeted for the upstream HELM rework. The old version edited
scripts/globals/hobbies/helm/data.lua, whose per-type `mod` field no longer
exists; break-reducing mods now live in the file-local `breakMods` table in
scripts/globals/hobbies/helm/logic.lua, and upstream leaves Excavation out of
it (`[xi.helmType.EXCAVATION] = nil`).

There is still no EXCAVATION_RESULT mod, so point Excavation at the mining pair
the Field set already grants: MINING_RESULT_NQ (515) and MINING_RESULT_HQ (300),
which replaced the removed MINING_RESULT. Both are required: doesToolBreak only
applies a reduction when `mods[1] and mods[2]` are both set, so granting the NQ
mod alone would be a no-op.

Break chance only; yield is unaffected. Be aware the reworked formula is
multiplicative (0.893^nq * 0.843^hq) rather than additive, so a full Field set is
a substantially larger reduction than the pre-rework version delivered.
---
diff --git a/scripts/globals/hobbies/helm/logic.lua b/scripts/globals/hobbies/helm/logic.lua
index e6f2e80cba..57d95be483 100644
--- a/scripts/globals/hobbies/helm/logic.lua
+++ b/scripts/globals/hobbies/helm/logic.lua
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ local breakMods =
     [xi.helmType.HARVESTING] = { xi.mod.HARVESTING_RESULT_NQ, xi.mod.HARVESTING_RESULT_HQ },
     [xi.helmType.LOGGING]    = { xi.mod.LOGGING_RESULT_NQ, xi.mod.LOGGING_RESULT_HQ },
     [xi.helmType.MINING]     = { xi.mod.MINING_RESULT_NQ, xi.mod.MINING_RESULT_HQ },
-    [xi.helmType.EXCAVATION] = nil,
+    [xi.helmType.EXCAVATION] = { xi.mod.MINING_RESULT_NQ, xi.mod.MINING_RESULT_HQ },
 }
 
 local function getDropWeight(player, zoneId, zoneInfo, drop)
